{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you all for those findings. Let me make sure I understand what's been entered into the record today. Ms. Patel, you've reported that more than 18 students creates crowding issues for effective supervision — I'll enter that as a formal finding. Mr. Rivera, you've confirmed the Library Annex is already reserved for literacy tutoring on Tuesdays and Thursdays, but is available on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays — entered as a formal finding. And Ms. Chen, you've confirmed that current youth-protection clearance is required for every adult supervising the center, and that only two staff — Ms. Rivera and Mr. Chen — are cleared and available for all three proposed operating days — entered as a formal finding.

Now let me note what this means for the operating plan. The draft proposed Tuesdays and Thursdays in the Library Annex, but Mr. Rivera's finding shows those days are already taken. Since the center requires three operating days per week, we'd need to use the Annex on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays instead. Ms. Chen's finding tells us we need cleared staff for all three of those days, and only Ms. Rivera and Mr. Chen are cleared and available. And Ms. Patel's finding suggests our enrollment limit should be no more than 18, not 24, to ensure effective supervision.

Before I settle on a final plan, does anyone have additional findings or concerns to enter into the record?"}

